    {
      "id": "xxh-3-64-bits-5f8fa5",
      "name": "XXH3_64bits",
      "category": "xxhash",
      "signature": "XXH3_64bits(Data, Len)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Data",
          "type": "void*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Len",
          "type": "size_t"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "XXH64_hash_t",
      "docs": "-**********************************************************************\nXXH3 64-bit variant\n**********************************************************************"
    },
    {
      "id": "xxh-3-64-bits-with-seed-c421ad",
      "name": "XXH3_64bits_withSeed",
      "category": "xxhash",
      "signature": "XXH3_64bits_withSeed(Data, Len, Seed)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Data",
          "type": "void*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Len",
          "type": "size_t"
        },
        {
          "name": "Seed",
          "type": "XXH64_hash_t"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "XXH64_hash_t",
      "docs": "XXH3_64bits_withSeed():\nThis variant generates a custom secret on the fly\nbased on default secret altered using the `seed` value.\nWhile this operation is decently fast, note that it's not completely free.\nNote: seed==0 produces the same results as XXH3_64bits()."
    },
    {
      "id": "xxh-3-64-bits-with-secret-0c1ede",
      "name": "XXH3_64bits_withSecret",
      "category": "xxhash",
      "signature": "XXH3_64bits_withSecret(Data, Len, Secret, Secret Size)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Data",
          "type": "void*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Len",
          "type": "size_t"
        },
        {
          "name": "Secret",
          "type": "void*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Secret Size",
          "type": "size_t"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "XXH64_hash_t",
      "docs": "XXH3_64bits_withSecret():\nIt's possible to provide any blob of bytes as a \"secret\" to generate the hash.\nThis makes it more difficult for an external actor to prepare an intentional collision.\nThe main condition is that secretSize *must* be large enough (>= XXH3_SECRET_SIZE_MIN).\nHowever, the quality of produced hash values depends on secret's entropy.\nTechnically, the secret must look like a bunch of random bytes.\nAvoid \"trivial\" or structured data such as repeated sequences or a text document.\nWhenever unsure about the \"randomness\" of the blob of bytes,\nconsider relabelling it as a \"custom seed\" instead,\nand employ \"XXH3_generateSecret()\" (see below)\nto generate a high entropy secret derived from the custom seed."
    },
