    {
      "id": "xxh-3-64-bits-reset-with-seed",
      "name": "XXH3_64bits_reset_withSeed",
      "category": "xxhash",
      "signature": "XXH3_64bits_reset_withSeed(State Ptr, Seed)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "State Ptr",
          "type": "XXH3_state_t*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Seed",
          "type": "XXH64_hash_t"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "XXH_errorcode",
      "docs": "XXH3_64bits_reset_withSeed():\nGenerate a custom secret from `seed`, and store it into `statePtr`.\ndigest will be equivalent to `XXH3_64bits_withSeed()`."
    },
    {
      "id": "xxh-3-64-bits-reset-with-secret",
      "name": "XXH3_64bits_reset_withSecret",
      "category": "xxhash",
      "signature": "XXH3_64bits_reset_withSecret(State Ptr, Secret, Secret Size)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "State Ptr",
          "type": "XXH3_state_t*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Secret",
          "type": "void*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Secret Size",
          "type": "size_t"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "XXH_errorcode",
      "docs": "XXH3_64bits_reset_withSecret():\n`secret` is referenced, it _must outlive_ the hash streaming session.\nSimilar to one-shot API, `secretSize` must be >= `XXH3_SECRET_SIZE_MIN`,\nand the quality of produced hash values depends on secret's entropy\n(secret's content should look like a bunch of random bytes).\nWhen in doubt about the randomness of a candidate `secret`,\nconsider employing `XXH3_generateSecret()` instead (see below)."
    },
